    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (2 tests, 0 failures). `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change derives a read-only `contactPreference` field on the owner response: `EMAIL` when an email is present, otherwise `PHONE`.\n\n**Where the logic went** \u2014 I kept it consistent with how the other derived owner fields (`displayName`, `locality`, `membershipLevel`, \u2026) are already handled:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `contactPreference` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"contactPreference\", expression = \"java(resolveContactPreference(owner))\")` and a small `resolveContactPreference(Owner)` method returning `\"EMAIL\"`/`\"PHONE\"`. Rather than duplicating the email-presence check, I extracted the existing inline logic from `resolveMembershipLevel` into a shared private `hasEmail(Owner)` helper and reused it in both places.\n\nNo new class or catch-all was needed \u2014 the presence-of-email check now lives in one small, single-responsibility helper shared by the two derivations that depend on it.",
